Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.71,0:00:33.16,Default,,0,1200,500,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs50}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b1}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.71,0:00:33.16,Sign - Copy,,750,0,475,,{\b1}Return to a Nation \N with an Uncertain Future{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.72,0:00:36.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The air raids have started again!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.52,0:00:40.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Did anyone manage to tap into the\Nsubmarine crew's comm network?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.12,0:00:41.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.42,0:00:44.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There aren't any frequencies we can tap into.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.32,0:00:45.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.72,0:00:49.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,consolidate all available\Ndisposable territories in cyberspace
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.22,0:00:52.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and clear enough space for the memories\Nand ghosts of three million people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.82,0:00:53.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.82,0:00:55.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where did this come from!?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.92,0:00:57.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.12,0:00:57.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Do it ASAP.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.02,0:01:01.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But, but... Is that even possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.42,0:01:02.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.72,0:01:05.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't think of any other way\Nto save the refugees, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.02,0:01:06.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.83,0:01:08.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,R-R-Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.93,0:01:15.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have my support AIs working to secure\Na disposable territory in cyberspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.33,0:01:18.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's begin once preparations are complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.63,0:01:19.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.13,0:01:22.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even supposing that we survive
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.73,0:01:25.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by transferring our ghosts to the net,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.43,0:01:27.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,what about those who don't have cyberbrains?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.43,0:01:32.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,For refugees who have\Nrelatives without cyberbrains,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.43,0:01:34.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,our proposal will be difficult to accept.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.43,0:01:37.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They will lose trust in me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.73,0:01:39.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and voluntarily leave Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.93,0:01:42.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In this kind of situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.73,0:01:46.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the role of a leader is great\Nand full of uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.13,0:01:50.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You must sometimes make\Nsituational decisions by yourself,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.63,0:01:53.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,especially in positions where\Nyou must lead many people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.93,0:01:56.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm sure they understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.53,0:02:00.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I... hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.00,0:02:05.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.00,0:02:07.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is the shortest route\Nto the Major's location?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.20,0:02:10.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Batou-San! Didn't you head for the bridge?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.60,0:02:12.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have to go get the Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.46,0:02:15.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Batou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.66,0:02:17.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The comm link...!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.76,0:02:26.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder if they'll take advantage of\Nthe air raid chaos to fire the missile?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.66,0:02:30.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since the nuclear sub isn't\Ntransmitting any messages,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.76,0:02:33.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,maybe the launch time is already decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.56,0:02:34.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.46,0:02:39.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,judging from the Aegis distance from Dejima,\Nand the micro-machine dispersal timing,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.86,0:02:42.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it'll probably be around 1000 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.16,0:02:49.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey everyone, what do you guys really think?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.16,0:02:51.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Do you really believe the\Nrefugees ghosts would be preserved
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.76,0:02:54.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by uploading their memories to the net?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.16,0:03:01.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Memories are important factors in life,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.46,0:03:04.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but they're just data without a ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.46,0:03:08.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But didn't the Major decide\Nto pin her hopes on that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.56,0:03:10.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, I understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.06,0:03:12.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But her order is too reckless!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.56,0:03:13.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.36,0:03:18.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But we can't save Batou-San and\Nthe others if we do what she says.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.56,0:03:22.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, I think I'll ignore her order.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.35,0:03:25.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?! Ignore her order?\NWhat the...? What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.65,0:03:25.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What are we going to do about Dejima?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.87,0:03:28.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How is it going?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.57,0:03:29.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's not working.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.17,0:03:32.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They aren't responding to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.07,0:03:35.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The hotline is open, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.17,0:03:38.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.17,0:03:39.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.37,0:03:41.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is frustrating.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.07,0:03:47.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's true that I was just a figurehead\Nadvanced to win the snap election,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.07,0:03:50.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but that's no reason to treat me this way!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.34,0:03:57.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If Takakura will go this far,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.54,0:04:01.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll settle this... my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.44,0:04:02.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Whom will you contact?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.59,0:04:10.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.79,0:04:12.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is the eighth!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.59,0:04:15.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We rock at this kind of computation!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.49,0:04:16.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.69,0:04:20.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can definitely put up a barrage in the\Nmissile's trajectory with just one more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.69,0:04:23.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Just like you said, it was the right\Nchoice to ignore the Major's order
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.99,0:04:26.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and bet on making the satellites fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.79,0:04:28.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.29,0:04:30.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.39,0:04:31.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's going great.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.89,0:04:33.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.79,0:04:39.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This satellite may be the one with our AIs on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.49,0:04:41.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.29,0:04:44.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why? It's a satellite of the Empire!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.89,0:04:45.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.49,0:04:47.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.59,0:04:52.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it looks like we're using borrowed space on an\Nimperial satellite that was launched from Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.29,0:04:54.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:58.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're at their mercy whether we have\Nthe Security Pact with them or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.69,0:05:02.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Anyway, why did the Major put our AIs there?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.89,0:05:03.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.79,0:05:07.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe we were trying to spy on them?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.79,0:05:10.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can't be sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.09,0:05:10.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But what now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.59,0:05:12.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We don't have time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.18,0:05:25.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ishikawa-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.58,0:05:26.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.68,0:05:31.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have to go somewhere with everyone...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.07,0:05:37.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.77,0:05:38.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.97,0:05:40.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.17,0:05:42.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Take care of the Major and the others for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.27,0:05:43.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.07,0:05:47.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Okay,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.47,0:05:50.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess I'm really on my own now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.17,0:05:56.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.17,0:05:58.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.06,0:06:09.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.16,0:06:10.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.26,0:06:12.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can you... fold cranes?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.96,0:06:13.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Cranes?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.86,0:06:15.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.26,0:06:17.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and using only your left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.26,0:06:23.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Anyone can if he uses control software, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.26,0:06:24.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I didn't mean it like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.36,0:06:31.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can you fold cranes using only your left hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.76,0:06:32.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Now I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.36,0:06:38.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You seem to be someone who\Nhas also survived solitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.56,0:06:42.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I haven't asked you for your name; what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.36,0:06:44.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.36,0:06:46.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,though I do have an alias.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.26,0:06:49.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Aren't you the same?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.66,0:06:50.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.96,0:06:54.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugees gave me several names.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.96,0:06:58.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I thought I was working with them to save them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.46,0:07:01.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but perhaps I was just staying with them...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.56,0:07:03.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to alleviate my own solitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.86,0:07:06.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But in the end, it didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.16,0:07:09.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even though they depended on you,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.36,0:07:11.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you couldn't depend on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.96,0:07:16.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Do you have people you can trust?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.26,0:07:18.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.56,0:07:24.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.96,0:07:29.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I... have been looking for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.82,0:07:42.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It'll be fine; missiles won't\Ntarget areas near the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.42,0:07:44.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't panic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.87,0:08:55.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Motoko...!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.00,0:09:28.10,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}We're all alive.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.20,0:09:32.10,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}It's because we're all alive that we're sad.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.20,0:09:40.10,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}When we raise our hands and let\Nthe sunlight filter through,{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.10,0:09:47.09,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}we can see our blood coursing\Nthrough them a vivid red.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.10,0:09:51.80,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}Even earthworms, mole crickets{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.65,0:09:53.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh my god...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.90,0:09:56.10,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}and water striders{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.55,0:09:57.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You all must have... ghosts within you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.20,0:09:59.90,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}are all, all alive{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.27,0:10:00.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong, Proto?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.00,0:10:03.40,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}and all our friends.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.50,0:10:07.70,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}We're all alive.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.80,0:10:11.80,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}It's because we're all alive that we laugh.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.90,0:10:15.70,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}We're all alive.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.80,0:10:19.70,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}It's because we're all alive that we're glad.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.80,0:10:27.40,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}When we raise our hands and let\Nthe sunlight filter through,{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.50,0:10:34.70,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}we can see our blood coursing\Nthrough them a vivid red.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.80,0:10:39.30,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}Even dragonflies, frogs,{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.40,0:10:43.70,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}and honey bees{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.80,0:10:48.90,Default,,0,0,850,,{\i1\b1\c&H0000FF&\fs50\shad6}are all, all alive and all our fr...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.93,0:10:53.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong, Proto?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.33,0:10:54.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.03,0:10:59.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems the Tachikoma used the satellite\Ncontaining their AIs to block the nuclear missile,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.83,0:11:01.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They did what...?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.83,0:11:04.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So we've managed to avert a total disaster?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.73,0:11:05.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.13,0:11:09.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm having difficulty grasping the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.33,0:11:11.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems we avoided a nuclear missile drop
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.63,0:11:14.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,thanks to my subordinates sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.23,0:11:14.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Your subordinates?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.73,0:11:17.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,More importantly, what did you do earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.94,0:11:24.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.23,0:11:27.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What, the missile?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.73,0:11:29.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Ah well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.23,0:11:34.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Either way, Kayabuki's actions\Nwill set the scene for a cold war.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.53,0:11:40.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, he failed to become a hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.03,0:11:45.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What was that explosion?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.33,0:11:49.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah... We heard the Tachikoma's song, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.13,0:11:51.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They stopped it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.40,0:12:09.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.60,0:12:10.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,For some reason,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.90,0:12:14.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the AIs seem to have acted\Ndifferently from my commands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.90,0:12:20.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, are you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.79,0:12:21.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Tachikoma...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.76,0:12:35.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief, if the Prime Minister contacted...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.76,0:12:37.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.26,0:12:40.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, securing the Chief Cabinet\NSecretary and Gouda has higher priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.56,0:12:46.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There is a possibility that we cannot get\Nthis out in the open while we're still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.96,0:12:49.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let us settle things swiftly first.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.66,0:12:50.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.14,0:12:56.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.41,0:13:00.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief Cabinet Secretary,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.11,0:13:04.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you are aware of our reason\Nfor coming here, are you not?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.81,0:13:06.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You attempted a coup d'etat,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.51,0:13:09.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,not to mention mass murder\Nunder the pretext of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.81,0:13:12.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We could not let a nuclear suicide-bombing occur.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.71,0:13:15.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There was no such thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.31,0:13:19.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You created that scenario with Gouda from\Nthe Cabinet Intelligence Agency, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.61,0:13:20.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.31,0:13:26.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I merely pushed the Security Pact\Nforward, for the good of the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.21,0:13:28.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is a war with the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.71,0:13:31.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Secretary!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.11,0:13:36.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This is an unofficial statement,\Nbut you are facing a rigorous inquiry.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.11,0:13:38.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm prepared for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.41,0:13:39.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,More importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.51,0:13:43.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it seems you were more of a\Nwoman than I thought you were.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.91,0:13:47.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't know who you ran to crying for help,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.31,0:13:50.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but this nation cannot survive\Nwithout the American Empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.21,0:13:54.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You seem to be mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.11,0:13:59.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It doesn't seem to have been a nuclear blast.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.41,0:14:00.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What shall we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.71,0:14:02.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Launch another one?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.61,0:14:03.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.61,0:14:08.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,let's wait until we can identify the targets\Nheading towards us from the northeast.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.21,0:14:12.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If they are marked with China's\Nmilitary flag, though...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.21,0:14:20.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,"National independence through\Npersonal independence."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.21,0:14:20.51,Default,,0,1200,875,,{\fs40}{\b1\i1}Note: This is a famous quote by Fukuzawa Yukichi, a Meiji-era enlightenment thinker and educator{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.51,0:14:27.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I consider myself to have acted in accordance\Nwith that principle from the very beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.11,0:14:30.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Kayabuki regime will continue as it has,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.21,0:14:36.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,pursuing independent decision-making and a multilateral\Napproach with the UN while maintaining an equal distance
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.91,0:14:41.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,from the American Empire, the Ameri-Russo Federation,\NChina, and the dual nations for Asia and the EU.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.21,0:14:57.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The ASDF's special ops...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.91,0:15:00.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have confirmed Japan's intent in this matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.31,0:15:01.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We will retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.60,0:15:04.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Take him away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.30,0:15:05.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.09,0:15:13.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We came at the Prime Minister's orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.89,0:15:15.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please get on!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.29,0:15:16.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.59,0:15:18.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Stand up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.79,0:15:22.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll be taking this back now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.48,0:15:34.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Saitou, Pazu, Bomer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.38,0:15:36.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, you're all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.98,0:15:37.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.48,0:15:42.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sorry to ask this of you, but report the\Ndetails of the circumstances to the SDF.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.18,0:15:43.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.59,0:15:58.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.31,0:16:15.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're Ishikawa from Section 9, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.31,0:16:17.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Give it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.71,0:16:20.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.31,0:16:21.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.95,0:16:28.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't mess with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.85,0:16:32.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Section 9's good at both\Nintelligence and knocking heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.89,0:16:39.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If the land of slaves doesn't deliver on services,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.49,0:16:42.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the land that consumes their\Nservices will necessarily starve.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.39,0:16:45.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Labour shortages will benefit the\Nindustry that manufactures slaves,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.59,0:16:49.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but if the industries demand their rights too much,\Nthe flow of capitalism will slow down to a trickle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.49,0:16:54.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,My nation has declared itself capitalist,\Nat least intellectually by its "brain",
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.29,0:16:57.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but in reality, it is an ideal socialist state.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.89,0:16:59.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Once waste products accumulate in the system,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.89,0:17:02.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,a brain that can manage the\Nallocation of blood becomes necessary,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.89,0:17:07.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I imagine that would be the same for your\Nnation, which advocates freedom and equality.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.69,0:17:08.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.99,0:17:11.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But appearance and reality\Nare two different things.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.29,0:17:13.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.49,0:17:15.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.26,0:17:25.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.76,0:17:28.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You don't want an early grave.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.36,0:17:31.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Aramaki-San.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.56,0:17:32.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is this about?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.36,0:17:34.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda Kazundo.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.96,0:17:37.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You are charged with attempted\Nconspiracy to cause civil war,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.36,0:17:42.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and attempted conspiracy to\Nstart a war for personal gain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.66,0:17:44.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You will come with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.16,0:17:47.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Chief Cabinet Secretary has\Nadmitted this culpability as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.96,0:17:51.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, your last "production" ended in failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.16,0:17:52.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.66,0:17:55.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, there is no point in arresting me now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.06,0:17:57.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.46,0:18:02.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Chief Cabinet Secretary and\NI were always acting as standalones.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.46,0:18:08.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, the police should have already\Nreceived a report that I wrote myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.24,0:18:11.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You don't know about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.74,0:18:13.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Regarding those charges against me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.84,0:18:19.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,criminal law dictates that if the suspect turns\Nhimself in, he is acquitted of all charges.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.44,0:18:23.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will go to a nation that requires my talents.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.34,0:18:27.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you really sure about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.84,0:18:30.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have a document from the Prime Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.64,0:18:34.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,She thinks highly of your skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.84,0:18:38.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, if there is a possibility\Nthat you will leave the country,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.94,0:18:40.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we are to take any means necessary to prevent it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.44,0:18:45.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,She also says that, depending on the\Ncircumstances, we should be willing to kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.24,0:18:48.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is your decision?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.74,0:18:50.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't mind them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.04,0:18:52.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's just a threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.94,0:18:54.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.14,0:18:55.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.14,0:18:56.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh really?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.24,0:19:00.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then die!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.27,0:19:10.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Too bad for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.37,0:19:13.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.37,0:19:15.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're...!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.67,0:19:17.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You bastards!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.17,0:19:19.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How long were you involved in this deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.87,0:19:21.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.27,0:19:24.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hurry! We must not let them kill him!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.70,0:19:45.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.60,0:19:46.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A... crane.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.00,0:19:48.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Crane?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.10,0:19:52.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The micro-machine stuff works really\Nwell, that's for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.50,0:19:55.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can die painlessly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.00,0:19:58.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're a very interesting man,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.60,0:20:01.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but you're dangerous to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.60,0:20:05.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Your country does not need a charismatic\Nleader who cannot be controlled.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.80,0:20:08.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All we need are docile consumers.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.60,0:20:13.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll be going... first.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.19,0:20:34.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.49,0:20:36.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,where are you wasting time?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.59,0:20:40.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Rendezvous with Azuma and\NProto in Niihama Sector 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.69,0:20:41.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.89,0:20:44.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We got the additional budget you requested!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.79,0:20:47.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Uchikoma, information.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.89,0:20:48.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.13,0:20:53.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listen, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.03,0:20:56.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There were many casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.33,0:21:00.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugee problem merely returned to square one,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.33,0:21:03.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and Prime Minister Kayabuki's proposed\Nindependent-coalition approach
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.43,0:21:06.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,will be a difficult road for the people to follow.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.53,0:21:11.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,From now on, people like us will\Nbecome more necessary than ever before.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.23,0:21:12.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.23,0:21:15.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What? Hey, you're acting\Nlike it's not your problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.23,0:21:20.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, please don't tell us that you've\Ntaken a philosophical view on everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.03,0:21:28.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, we have a report that our budget went\N through at the 329th National Deliberative Assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.43,0:21:29.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.83,0:21:33.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll end our round-the-clock\Nobservation of cherry trees
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.63,0:21:35.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and return to our jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.73,0:21:36.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finally.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.03,0:21:37.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.63,0:21:40.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thought I'd die from boredom.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.23,0:21:43.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We should've warmed the units up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.33,0:21:45.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's more like you, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.73,0:21:47.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about the briefing?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.43,0:21:49.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Just do a dive?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.23,0:21:51.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No, go on ahead and lead the team.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.83,0:21:53.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll join you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.83,0:21:54.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.55,0:22:02.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.35,0:22:04.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.95,0:22:06.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing.
